<node id="O003">
  <data key="d31">Agentic Skill Decay</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Skills &amp; learning</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-skill-decay</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-skill-decay</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-skill-decay</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-08-31</data>
  <data key="d37">Developers must deliberately practice reasoning, debugging and code comprehension when agents perform most implementation work.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Preserve manual practice and counterfactual reasoning exercises; Measure retained comprehension rather than prompt throughput; Avoid confusing agent task success with human competence.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">Osmani describes how automatic completion can remove the repetitions that once built expertise. He proposes predicting failures before asking an agent, explaining diffs, reconstructing decisions and periodically solving problems manually so proficiency does not disappear behind apparent task completion.</data>
  <data key="d222">Developers must deliberately practice reasoning, debugging and code comprehension when agents perform most implementation work.</data>
  <data key="d223">Preserve manual practice and counterfactual reasoning exercises; Measure retained comprehension rather than prompt throughput; Avoid confusing agent task success with human competence.</data>
