<node id="O005">
  <data key="d31">Human judgment doesn't leave the software factory. It relocates.</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/human-judgment-doesnt-leave-the-software</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/human-judgment-doesnt-leave-the-software</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/human-judgment-doesnt-leave-the-software</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-08-21</data>
  <data key="d37">Agentic factories relocate human responsibility toward intent, quality criteria and authorization rather than eliminating it.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Put human judgment at the intention and acceptance boundaries; Automate early regression and security checks; Escalate design ambiguity and irreversible operations to authorized owners.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">The article compares human-supervised and largely unattended factories and asks who defines product intent, architectural trade-offs and unacceptable regressions. It advocates persistent checks, managed risk boundaries and explicit ownership even when many implementation steps run without a person present.</data>
  <data key="d222">Agentic factories relocate human responsibility toward intent, quality criteria and authorization rather than eliminating it.</data>
  <data key="d223">Put human judgment at the intention and acceptance boundaries; Automate early regression and security checks; Escalate design ambiguity and irreversible operations to authorized owners.</data>
  <data key="d42">2026</data>
  <data key="d50">11.6</data>
