<node id="O008">
  <data key="d31">Software Factories, Light and Dark</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-07-22</data>
  <data key="d37">A software factory is many governed loops; its level of human involvement changes both risk and total operating cost.</data>
  <data key="d38">A conceptual taxonomy and projections, not a controlled comparison of factory operating models.</data>
  <data key="d39">Separate an autonomous loop from the governance system supervising many loops; Measure cost of failures and rework, not just generation speed; Choose review intensity by reversibility and blast radius.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">The essay contrasts "light" factories that retain human interpretation with "dark" factories that minimize review, exposing the trade-off between throughput and lost comprehension. Osmani argues that harness capability and measurable verification should determine safe autonomy, not the attraction of unattended execution.</data>
  <data key="d222">A software factory is many governed loops; its level of human involvement changes both risk and total operating cost.</data>
  <data key="d223">Separate an autonomous loop from the governance system supervising many loops; Measure cost of failures and rework, not just generation speed; Choose review intensity by reversibility and blast radius.</data>
