<node id="O011">
  <data key="d31">Agentic Code Review</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-code-review</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-code-review</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-code-review</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-06-16</data>
  <data key="d37">AI-generated code moves the bottleneck from writing to justified acceptance, making review strategy a core engineering skill.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Allocate human attention by risk rather than diff size; Audit automated reviewer false positives and misses; Preserve review as a team knowledge-transfer mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">Osmani contrasts solo experiments and long-lived team repositories, arguing that risk, context, integration and shared learning demand different review methods. Review must consider correctness evidence, comprehension and how design decisions survive the handoff.</data>
  <data key="d222">AI-generated code moves the bottleneck from writing to justified acceptance, making review strategy a core engineering skill.</data>
  <data key="d223">Allocate human attention by risk rather than diff size; Audit automated reviewer false positives and misses; Preserve review as a team knowledge-transfer mechanism.</data>
