  <data key="d131">2026-04-30</data>
  <data key="d37">Agents operating across sessions require durable task state, resumability, recovery and verifiable progress.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Persist decisions and current state outside the transient model context; Make retries idempotent and restartable; Verify continuity and completion against external artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">The article examines context-window exhaustion, repeated mistakes and premature "done" claims in workflows lasting days. It recommends structured progress artifacts, checkpoints, clean workspaces and independent acceptance tests to support handoffs between agent sessions.</data>
  <data key="d222">Agents operating across sessions require durable task state, resumability, recovery and verifiable progress.</data>
  <data key="d223">Persist decisions and current state outside the transient model context; Make retries idempotent and restartable; Verify continuity and completion against external artifacts.</data>
