<node id="O014">
  <data key="d31">The Agent Stack Bet</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Code quality &amp; security</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/the-agent-stack-bet</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/the-agent-stack-bet</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/the-agent-stack-bet</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-04-18</data>
  <data key="d37">Production agents need identity, authorization, observability and recovery controls beyond an impressive base model.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Bind every action to scoped identity and human ownership; Restrict tool permissions and monitor effects; Design recoverable operations and audit trails for runtime failures.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">Osmani describes fragile production plumbing: broad service-account permissions, schema drift, opaque state and broken recovery. The remedy is an explicit agent stack with task-scoped access, traceability, policy enforcement and durable error handling.</data>
  <data key="d222">Production agents need identity, authorization, observability and recovery controls beyond an impressive base model.</data>
  <data key="d223">Bind every action to scoped identity and human ownership; Restrict tool permissions and monitor effects; Design recoverable operations and audit trails for runtime failures.</data>
