<node id="O018">
  <data key="d31">How to write a good spec for AI agents</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-01-19</data>
  <data key="d37">A useful agent specification is compact, testable and iterative rather than a giant prompt resembling an unvalidated requirements dump.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Specify desired behavior and forbidden regressions separately from implementation detail; Plan before writes, then build in small independently checked increments; Update specification when evidence reveals an ambiguity.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">Osmani provides guidance on the degree of detail in requirements, decomposition into small tasks, read-only planning and successive execution. Intent, constraints, expected behavior and testing guidance become checkpoints throughout development.</data>
  <data key="d222">A useful agent specification is compact, testable and iterative rather than a giant prompt resembling an unvalidated requirements dump.</data>
  <data key="d223">Specify desired behavior and forbidden regressions separately from implementation detail; Plan before writes, then build in small independently checked increments; Update specification when evidence reveals an ambiguity.</data>
  <data key="d42">2026</data>
  <data key="d50">4.1</data>
