<node id="O019">
  <data key="d31">Code Review in the Age of AI</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d35">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d36">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d126">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-01-05</data>
  <data key="d37">The rise in generated changes makes code review an explicit burden-of-proof and accountability process.</data>
  <data key="d38">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d39">Attach objective verification artifacts to pull requests; Review intent, integration risk and sensitive paths; Never treat a passing self-generated test as independent approval.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">The essay argues that tests, reproducible manual checks and a stated risk assessment should accompany every proposal. Teams should preserve contextual knowledge and ownership rather than confusing a model-generated diff with evidence that the resulting change is safe.</data>
  <data key="d222">The rise in generated changes makes code review an explicit burden-of-proof and accountability process.</data>
  <data key="d223">Attach objective verification artifacts to pull requests; Review intent, integration risk and sensitive paths; Never treat a passing self-generated test as independent approval.</data>
  <data key="d42">2026</data>
  <data key="d50">8.9</data>
  <data key="d224">C08</data>
  <data key="d225">Direct</data>
  <data key="d52">curated practitioner article (not a research study)</data>
  <data key="d226">false</data>
  <data key="d227">W065;W069;W093</data>
  <data key="d53">Osmani public Substack sitemaps 2024/2025/2026 plus individual source URLs; independent editorial review 2026-10-10</data>
  <data key="d55">Overlay only; does not change any original W001-W193 evidence classification</data>
  <data key="d228">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence. Any externally quoted benchmark, productivity or vendor telemetry requires independent verification of original method and population.</data>
  <data key="d229">yes</data>
  <data key="d48">https://addyo.substack.com/sitemap/2026</data>
  <data key="d49">Substack essay, not a peer-reviewed research paper</data>
  <data key="d230">REVISED</data>
  <data key="d231">true</data>
  <data key="d232">2026-10-10</data>
