  <data key="d184">https://addyo.substack.com/p/the-reality-of-ai-assisted-software</data>
  <data key="d131">2025-08-16</data>
  <data key="d37">Perceived personal acceleration with coding AI does not necessarily translate into net team or release-level productivity.</data>
  <data key="d38">The percentages reported by Osmani come from diverse third-party surveys and experiments; no single pooled causal estimate is supplied.</data>
  <data key="d39">Use task-adjusted and quality-adjusted metrics; Report study context before citing a percentage; Separate survey sentiment, experiments and shipped-value outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d40">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d44">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d43">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">The article synthesizes surveys and selected field studies showing variation by task, developer and codebase. It cautions against treating high adoption, code generation or self-reported speed as direct evidence of deployment throughput or organizational value.</data>
  <data key="d222">Perceived personal acceleration with coding AI does not necessarily translate into net team or release-level productivity.</data>
  <data key="d223">Use task-adjusted and quality-adjusted metrics; Report study context before citing a percentage; Separate survey sentiment, experiments and shipped-value outcomes.</data>
