  <data key="d41">A</data>
  <data key="d45">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d51">Osmani frames the assistant as a capable but fallible collaborator whose output must be tested and reviewed before adoption. The post translates automation-bias concerns into reviewer practices, guardrails and accountable sign-off.</data>
  <data key="d222">Verification becomes the bottleneck when generation is cheap; every AI-produced change needs a justified check.</data>
  <data key="d223">Check against independent requirements and regression oracles; Record the outcome of manual and automated review; Teach why plausible code is not proof of correctness.</data>
