  <data key="d261">[{"url": "https://blog.pragmaticengineer.com/ide-that-software-engineers-love/", "title": "Which IDEs do software engineers love, and why?", "date": "2024-11-26", "source_ref": "turn716629view0", "relation": "alternate_publication", "reason": "Author-confirmed excerpt/republication; retain the more complete canonical article."}]</data>
  <data key="d37">Reports a voluntary social-media poll about AI-enabled editors and discusses tool preferences.</data>
  <data key="d222">Reports a voluntary social-media poll about AI-enabled editors and discusses tool preferences.</data>
  <data key="d51">Reports a voluntary social-media poll about AI-enabled editors and discusses tool preferences. The canonical newsletter reports 155 responses; its public blog excerpt does not provide the whole newsletter.</data>
  <data key="d223">The poll describes early-adopter preferences, not industry market share or measured productivity. A conflicting 145-response sentence in the blog is retained as a source-edition discrepancy.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Voluntary replies across Bluesky, X and Threads; early-adopter self-selection. Canonical newsletter body and chart report 155 responses (77+62+16); one blog sentence says 145. Use 155 only as the canonical author-reported count, not an independently verified sample. The public blog supplies the IDE portion, not the complete newsletter, which also contains industry-news material. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Editor preference and adoption belong to workflow evidence, not causal productivity estimates or benchmarked capability.</data>
  <data key="d40">Industry/practitioner publication — self selected social media survey</data>
  <data key="d44">Industry/practitioner publication — self selected social media survey</data>
  <data key="d263">paid_preview_plus_public_excerpt</data>
  <data key="d264">Public preview and blog excerpt; complete newsletter not reviewed</data>
