  <data key="d37">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d222">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d51">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d223">Offers a useful contrast between shipping to learn and building for longevity. Reported business experiments are not evaluations of AI-assisted development.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Revenue and experimental effects are contributor-reported and not independently replicated here. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Growth engineering connects product hypotheses to measured outcomes rather than treating feature output as value.</data>
