  <data key="d37">Seven company accounts describe engineers building LLM products, including evaluation, nondeterminism, privacy, latency, bespoke tooling and usage-driven costs.</data>
  <data key="d222">Seven company accounts describe engineers building LLM products, including evaluation, nondeterminism, privacy, latency, bespoke tooling and usage-driven costs.</data>
  <data key="d51">Seven company accounts describe engineers building LLM products, including evaluation, nondeterminism, privacy, latency, bespoke tooling and usage-driven costs.</data>
  <data key="d223">The accessible cases distinguish easy prototypes from production obligations; they concern building AI products and cannot directly quantify coding-assistant productivity.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Orosz discloses investments in incident.io and Wordsmith, both included in the article. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">The cases concern building AI-enabled products; their operational lessons are not evidence of coding-agent productivity.</data>
