  <data key="d31">Stack overflow is almost dead</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_PEER_REVIEWED_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">System knowledge &amp; memory</data>
  <data key="d34">2025</data>
  <data key="d251">Gergely Orosz</data>
  <data key="d36">https://blog.pragmaticengineer.com/stack-overflow-is-almost-dead/</data>
  <data key="d126">https://blog.pragmaticengineer.com/stack-overflow-is-almost-dead/</data>
  <data key="d184">https://blog.pragmaticengineer.com/stack-overflow-is-almost-dead/</data>
  <data key="d131">2025-05-15</data>
  <data key="d252">Canonical article edition date; earlier identified parent-issue date retained separately</data>
  <data key="d253">2025-05-15</data>
  <data key="d254">2025-05-15</data>
  <data key="d255">CONFIRMED_RETITLED_PULSE_EXCERPT</data>
  <data key="d256">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/the-pulse-134</data>
  <data key="d257">false</data>
  <data key="d258">blog</data>
  <data key="d259">Blog</data>
  <data key="d260"></data>
  <data key="d261">[]</data>
  <data key="d37">Updates an earlier analysis of falling Stack Overflow question counts, considering moderation history, alternative communities and LLM-based assistance.</data>
  <data key="d222">Updates an earlier analysis of falling Stack Overflow question counts, considering moderation history, alternative communities and LLM-based assistance.</data>
  <data key="d51">Updates an earlier analysis of falling Stack Overflow question counts, considering moderation history, alternative communities and LLM-based assistance.</data>
  <data key="d223">The observations concern new questions, not all site usage or knowledge value. The headline and shutdown forecast go beyond what the descriptive series demonstrates.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Updated 19 May 2025. The causal contribution of LLMs is not identified by the time series. This non-Pulse-titled blog article is an excerpt of a Pulse issue originally published 2025-05-15. It passes the literal title-prefix rule; it is excluded by the optional stricter Pulse-origin filter. The parent issue is provenance only, not another P article. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">The follow-up concerns knowledge-community activity; fewer questions do not prove disappearance of all usage or knowledge value.</data>
  <data key="d40">Industry/practitioner publication — secondary data commentary</data>
