  <data key="d51">The survey reports tool usage and sentiment across languages, coding assistants, IDEs, delivery infrastructure and cloud platforms.</data>
  <data key="d223">This is a self-selected readership sample with 2,997 retained responses, not a random industry census. Cross-year differences can reflect changing respondents.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Same dataset as Parts 2 and 3; do not interpret mentions as causal productivity effects. The reported gross 3,000-plus submissions and cleaned 2,997 retained responses refer to stages of the same reader survey, not separate datasets. No microdata recount was performed. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">A broad, self-selected technology-stack survey with an AI-tooling subsection. Retain AI as a secondary facet; the same respondents underlie Parts 2 and 3.</data>
