  <data key="d51">Quentin Pradet examines API-first design, SDK generation, documentation and ongoing maintenance for human and model consumers.</data>
  <data key="d223">Clear contracts and robust libraries reduce integration friction; translating an SDK with an LLM does not remove language-specific correctness and maintenance work.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">A section explicitly discusses LLM-assisted SDK generation; it is secondary to the broader SDK design guidance. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">SDK contracts and reusable interfaces support maintainable systems without directly measuring AI-generated code quality.</data>
