  <data key="d256"></data>
  <data key="d257">true</data>
  <data key="d258">newsletter</data>
  <data key="d259">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d260"></data>
  <data key="d261">[]</data>
  <data key="d37">Laura Tacho presents company measurement practices combining adoption, delivery, quality and developer experience, with baseline and segmentation guidance.</data>
  <data key="d222">Laura Tacho presents company measurement practices combining adoption, delivery, quality and developer experience, with baseline and segmentation guidance.</data>
  <data key="d51">Laura Tacho presents company measurement practices combining adoption, delivery, quality and developer experience, with baseline and segmentation guidance.</data>
  <data key="d223">Metrics should constrain one another: output alone cannot establish net value. The framework and cases are practitioner evidence, not a new randomized evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">At publication Orosz disclosed investment in DX and Tacho was DX CTO; article states it was not sponsored. The source discloses Laura Tacho’s DX role and Orosz’s investment in DX. Company measurement practices are not a new randomized causal estimate. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Multi-company measurement practices combine delivery, quality and developer experience; commercial affiliations remain explicit.</data>
  <data key="d40">Industry/practitioner publication — multi company measurement report</data>
  <data key="d44">Industry/practitioner publication — multi company measurement report</data>
  <data key="d263">public_text</data>
