  <data key="d51">Orosz revisits Brooks’s distinction between fundamental software difficulty and tool-level improvement. The preview weighs AI against earlier developments such as reliability engineering, open source and collaboration tools.</data>
  <data key="d223">Large increases in generated code are not automatically comparable gains in productivity, reliability or simplicity. The historical comparison is an argument, not a controlled test.</data>
