<node id="P113">
  <data key="d31">Software engineering at a proprietary trading company: Optiver</data>
  <data key="d32">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d54">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_PEER_REVIEWED_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d33">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d34">2026</data>
  <data key="d251">Gergely Orosz; Ivan Klaric; Jesse Spevack</data>
  <data key="d36">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/optiver</data>
  <data key="d126">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/optiver</data>
  <data key="d184">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/optiver</data>
  <data key="d131">2026-08-11</data>
  <data key="d252">Canonical article edition date; earlier identified parent-issue date retained separately</data>
  <data key="d253">2026-08-11</data>
  <data key="d254">2026-08-11</data>
  <data key="d255">NO_PULSE_ORIGIN_IDENTIFIED</data>
  <data key="d256"></data>
  <data key="d257">true</data>
  <data key="d258">newsletter</data>
  <data key="d259">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d260"></data>
  <data key="d261">[]</data>
  <data key="d37">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption.</data>
  <data key="d222">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption.</data>
  <data key="d51">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption. The public introduction contrasts low-latency execution with increasingly important predictive models.</data>
  <data key="d223">Speed is constrained by the consequences of failure. Trading-specific architecture and incentives are useful boundary conditions, not a template for every development team.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38"> Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Trading-system constraints provide an important boundary case for engineering controls; do not generalize domain-specific incentives.</data>
