  <data key="d37">Interviews with Ramp describe a background coding agent running in remote sandboxes with internal integrations and backend/frontend verification.</data>
  <data key="d222">Interviews with Ramp describe a background coding agent running in remote sandboxes with internal integrations and backend/frontend verification.</data>
  <data key="d51">Interviews with Ramp describe a background coding agent running in remote sandboxes with internal integrations and backend/frontend verification. The preview explains why local-tool and context limitations motivated an internal platform.</data>
  <data key="d223">Remote environments and company context can matter as much as model selection. Adoption and self-verification claims are reported by the company, not controlled evidence of correctness.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38">Agent-origin merged-PR share is not a quality-adjusted productivity measure. Self-run tests and screenshots do not by themselves establish an independent acceptance oracle. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">The Inspect case emphasizes company context, remote sandboxes and verification; reported self-checks are not independent accuracy evidence.</data>
