  <data key="d259">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d260"></data>
  <data key="d261">[]</data>
  <data key="d37">The article surveys responses to growing AI-generated review workloads: reviewing AI feedback, routing by blast radius, inspecting plans and tests, reducing patch size, and retaining manual review.</data>
  <data key="d222">The article surveys responses to growing AI-generated review workloads: reviewing AI feedback, routing by blast radius, inspecting plans and tests, reducing patch size, and retaining manual review.</data>
  <data key="d51">The article surveys responses to growing AI-generated review workloads: reviewing AI feedback, routing by blast radius, inspecting plans and tests, reducing patch size, and retaining manual review.</data>
  <data key="d223">The visible discussion rejects a universal review process. Noise filtering, scope decisions and release responsibility remain important even when review automation increases.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38"> Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Reported review approaches depend on risk, noise and team context; the article does not validate one universal review policy.</data>
  <data key="d40">Industry/practitioner publication — reported practitioner analysis</data>
  <data key="d44">Industry/practitioner publication — reported practitioner analysis</data>
  <data key="d263">paid_preview</data>
  <data key="d264">Public preview/outline only; subscriber remainder not reviewed</data>
  <data key="d265">PROVISIONAL_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_CLASSIFICATION</data>
  <data key="d266">Reported review approaches depend on risk, noise and team context; the article does not validate one universal review policy.</data>
  <data key="d225">AI_FOR_SE</data>
  <data key="d267">not_presented_as_peer_reviewed</data>
