  <data key="d51">Interviews with Microsoft staff outline agent identity, local MCP discovery, isolation, local-model support and developer experience on Windows. The public portion also compares several differently sampled operating-system surveys.</data>
  <data key="d223">Agent identity and isolation are distinct from model capability. Survey populations and multiple-choice designs differ; stated platform plans are not independent security evaluations.</data>
  <data key="d262">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d38"> Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d39">Windows platform architecture enables AI applications and agents through identity, isolation and discovery. Distinguish roadmap features from deployed capabilities, and architecture from validated security outcomes.</data>
